From: The open-edison contributors
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: spidev: don't force SPI_CS_HIGH for ACPI devices

spidev sets SPI_CS_HIGH whenever the chip select is a GPIO descriptor (and
hides it when reading the mode), relying on gpiolib to apply the GPIO's
polarity. For ACPI devices the SPI core doesn't: it treats the GPIO as
active high and inverts it itself (spi_toggle_csgpiod()), so setting any
mode through spidev left the chip select active high.

Seen on the Intel Edison (Merrifield SPI5 with cs-gpios from ACPI): after
SPI_IOC_WR_MODE the chip select idled low and went high during transfers.

Only force (and hide) SPI_CS_HIGH for non-ACPI devices.
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spidev.c b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
index 4d53c39..4967cc2 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spidev.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <linux/mod_devicetable.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/acpi.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/compat.h>
@@ -380,7 +381,8 @@ spidev_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
 	case SPI_IOC_RD_MODE32:
 		tmp = spi->mode & SPI_MODE_MASK;
 
-		if (ctlr->use_gpio_descriptors && spi_get_csgpiod(spi, 0))
+		if (ctlr->use_gpio_descriptors && spi_get_csgpiod(spi, 0) &&
+		    !is_acpi_device_node(dev_fwnode(&spi->dev)))
 			tmp &= ~SPI_CS_HIGH;
 
 		if (cmd == SPI_IOC_RD_MODE)
@@ -414,7 +416,14 @@ spidev_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
 				break;
 			}
 
-			if (ctlr->use_gpio_descriptors && spi_get_csgpiod(spi, 0))
+			/*
+			 * gpiolib applies a GPIO chip select's polarity for DT; for
+			 * ACPI the SPI core treats the GPIO as active high and inverts
+			 * it itself (spi_toggle_csgpiod()), so forcing SPI_CS_HIGH here
+			 * would invert the chip select.
+			 */
+			if (ctlr->use_gpio_descriptors && spi_get_csgpiod(spi, 0) &&
+			    !is_acpi_device_node(dev_fwnode(&spi->dev)))
 				tmp |= SPI_CS_HIGH;
 
 			tmp |= spi->mode & ~SPI_MODE_MASK;
